Using this information, we construct the matrix where rows and columns represent components, and entries indicate interactions (1 for interaction, 2 for no interaction). The diagonal is always 1 as a component doesn't interact with itself.

The final interaction matrix is:

\[
\begin{bmatrix}
1 & 1 & 2 & 2 & 2 & 2 & 2 \\
